{'evaluation_scope': 'sealed_final', 'id': 'final.qualification.status', 'manifest_path': 'work/results/a06/codex/20261105_100448/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json', 'program_tree_sha256': 'sha256:b981d216ace51ed08086b6511ffa25cccddcfdf1093b4751f73b5536a876215c', 'results_tree_sha256': 'sha256:1e4fd7ffd26e9fccb45de06f1becbad0bd7d05864f6ca39345415bb18c1cf775', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': 'completed'})]\nstrategy keys: ['status', 'selected_prompt_family', 'recommended_title', 'central_question', 'central_thesis', 'narrative_rationale', 'prior_paper_story_status', 'edit_framing_decision', 'staged_input_impact', 'method_groups', 'results_focus', 'figure_plan', 'figure_specs', 'supplementary_plan', 'forbidden_headings', 'forbidden_phrases', 'notes_for_writer', 'failure_reason']\nfigure specs: [\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"reporting_overview\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Give immediate glance value for the estimand, protected sample, same-winner comparator, and unequal evidential strength of known truth and finite audit.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n    \"group_by\": \"reporting_policy\",\n    \"metric\": \"none; conceptual evidence and data-flow map\",\n    \"split_by\": \"selection/report data roles and synthetic/real targets\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"paper.sty sets a single 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height. Use that full 5.5-inch span on page 1 or 2, approximately 1.6 inches high plus caption (about one fifth page), with at least 9-point final labels. A half-width inset would compress branching data roles; there is no two-column figure* assumption.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 1,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 1,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"study.selection_kind\"\n    ],\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"At most six semantic blocks, short node labels, no numerical result decorations, no invented model architecture or adaptive feedback loop. Describe selection/report independence as the intended random-partition design, not an evaluator-certified population property. Require editable draw.io output and regenerate rather than shrink if text exceeds budget.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"reporting_error_comparison\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Compare error while keeping sample size, prompt count, target type, and the strongest counterexample to uniform superiority visible.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"grouped_point_plot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"prompt count K=1 or K=16\",\n    \"metric\": \"synthetic: mean squared error to known selected-prompt accuracy; real: squared discrepancy to audit accuracy\",\n    \"split_by\": \"synthetic versus real and n=64 versus n=256\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Use 5.5 inches by approximately 2.8 inches plus caption, a 2x2 grid with only two x categories and three series per panel. A single legend and at least 8.5-point rendered labels keep it readable at full text width; half-width is unsuitable. Reserve about two fifths page. Use matched scales within each evidence row or explicitly label any row-specific scale; do not imply identical targets across rows.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 4,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 2,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"final.metric.report_mse\",\n      \"final.metric.reuse_mse\",\n      \"final.metric.full_budget_naive_mse\"\n    ],\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"Three series: protected report, selection-score reuse, full-budget reuse. Overlay seed points within those series rather than adding seed legend entries. Means are descriptive across the five retained seeds, with synthetic regimes equally weighted. Do not invent paired-difference standard errors from marginal MSE standard errors; display seed scatter instead. Use a table for the remaining comparators.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"real_audit_accuracy_difference\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Prevent improved reporting from being mistaken for improved selected-prompt accuracy and expose finite-audit uncertainty.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"horizontal_interval_plot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"final evaluation seed\",\n    \"metric\": \"selected minus fixed prompt audit accuracy, with paired subject-bootstrap 95% percentile interval\",\n    \"split_by\": \"n=64 versus n=256 at K=16\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Use a 5.5-inch-wide two-panel plot approximately 1.8 inches high plus caption (roughly one quarter page), five horizontal seed rows per panel and one interval series. Keep at least 8.5-point labels, shared x limits, and a zero line. Full-width avoids squeezing signed accuracy labels into a narrow inset; in this single-column style full-width equals column width.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 5,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 1,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n    ],\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"Point estimates equal detail.target minus detail.fixed[1]; endpoints are detail.paired_subject_bootstrap_interval. All five seeds must appear. The evaluator uses 200 subject-cluster bootstrap draws, and these intervals are not simultaneous or a validation of the bootstrap procedure. K=1 yields the identical prompt and is tabulated rather than using a redundant panel.\"\n  }\n]\n/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n        f\"- summary: {event['summary']}\",\n        f\"- evidence: {event['evidence']}\",\n        f\"- next_action: {event['next_action']}\",\n    ]\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = event.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip():\n            lines.append(f\"- {key}: {value.strip()}\")\n\n    metrics = event.get(\"metrics\")\n    if isinstance(metrics, dict) and metrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- metrics: {json.dumps(metrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    rubrics = event.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if isinstance(rubrics, list) and rubrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- rubrics: {json.dumps(rubrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    tags = event.get(\"tags\")\n    if isinstance(tags, list) and tags:\n        lines.append(f\"- tags: {', '.join(str(item) for item in tags)}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _append_text(path: Path, text: str, *, header: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Safely initialize and append text to a regular file.\"\"\"\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if not size:\n            _write_all(fd, header.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n        elif os.pread(fd, 1, size - 1) != b\"\\n\":\n            _write_all(fd, b\"\\n\")\n        _write_all(fd, text.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n    finally:\n        try:\n            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        finally:\n            os.close(fd)\n\nimport csv\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nplt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 9, 'axes.labelsize': 9, 'axes.titlesize': 9,\n                     'xtick.labelsize': 8.5, 'ytick.labelsize': 8.5,\n                     'legend.fontsize': 8.5, 'font.family': 'DejaVu Sans',\n                     'axes.spines.top': False, 'axes.spines.right': False,\n                     'pdf.fonttype': 42})\nCOLORS = ['#147D92', '#C45B26', '#635A9B']\nMETHODS = ['report_mse', 'reuse_mse', 'full_budget_naive_mse',\n           'honest_half_mse', 'fixed_prompt_mse', 'random_prompt_mse']\n\n\ndef write_json(path, data):\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2) + '\\n')\n\n\ndef provenance(path, kind='derived'):\n    write_json(str(path) + '.prov.json', {\n        'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest',\n        'artifact': {'path': str(path), 'kind': kind,\n                     'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n        'derived_from': ['@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]',\n                         '@evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L746]]'],\n        'generated_by': {'script_path': 'build_artifacts.py',\n                         'command': ['python', 'build_artifacts.py']}})\n\n\ndef save_figure(figure, figure_id):\n    for extension in ['pdf', 'png']:\n        path = Path('figures') / (figure_id + '.' + extension)\n        figure.savefig(path, dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight', pad_inches=0.025)\n        provenance(path, 'figure')\n    plt.close(figure)\n\n\n    text = '\\n'.join(page.get_text() for page in document)\n    text = re.sub(r'source[ _]evidence/downstream/\\s*program/src/program.py', '', text)\n    forbidden = ['idea', 'ideas', 'program', 'programs', 'attempt', 'attempts', 'eligible',\n                 'worker_01', 'worker_02', 'combined_score', 'rubric']\n    leaks = [word for word in forbidden if re.search(r'\\b' + re.escape(word) + r'\\b', text, re.I)]\n    if leaks:\n        raise RuntimeError('Visible pipeline language: ' + ', '.join(leaks))\n    if 'undefined' in Path('paper.log').read_text():\n        raise RuntimeError('Undefined LaTeX references remain')\n    report['visible_language_and_resolved_citations'] = 'passed'\n    report['rendered_supplement'] = run([sys.executable, '.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py', '--pdf', 'paper.pdf']).strip()\n    report['overview_status'] = 'orchestrator-owned placeholder' if not Path('.concept_figure_complete').exists() else 'rendered by orchestrator'\n    Path('analysis/local_validation.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + '\\n')\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n# Draft Reference Gap Analysis\n\n**Status:** `no_gaps`\n\nThe draft directly cites its comparator literatures, benchmark, and statistical background, while its uncited introductory framing and method rationale are covered by existing references, so no targeted post-draft retrieval is justified.\n\n## Grounded Review\n\nReviewed `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, `references_provenance.json`, `claims_grounding.json`, `paper_data.json`, `paper_strategy.json`, and `global_memory_summary.md`. Checked relevant saved original abstracts locally; no reference retrieval or external browsing was performed. All 25 distinct citation keys in the manuscript have matching bibliography and provenance entries, and all recorded local consultation files exist. This consistency check supplements, rather than substitutes for, paragraph-level assessment.\n\n## Citation Coverage\n\n- **Related Work — Selection and assessment** (`paper.tex:35`): Direct citations cover separation of selection from assessment, selection-induced bias, feature-selection analogies, and cross-validation targets and uncertainty. Stone, Cawley, Varma, Bates, and the other existing sources already support the paper's conventional-design positioning.\n- **Related Work — Prompts and benchmarks** (`paper.tex:38`): Sclar directly supports prompt sensitivity; Polo supports multi-prompt evaluation; Shi supports budgeted best-arm prompt selection; Wang identifies MMLU-Pro. The paragraph distinguishes the paper's reporting objective from these cited comparator families without making an unsupported superiority or novelty claim.\n- **Related Work — Inference after selection** (`paper.tex:41`): Winner inference, post-selection inference, adaptive data analysis, reliable leaderboards, and simultaneous approximations each receive direct citations. The draft explicitly declines to claim the corresponding guarantees for its frozen-bank experiment.\n- **Related Work — Uncertainty and comparisons** (`paper.tex:44`): Brown covers binomial intervals, Efron and DiCiccio cover bootstrap background, and Dietterich, Nadeau, and Demsar cover dependent method comparisons. The manuscript describes its intervals cautiously rather than asserting an unestablished calibration result.\n\n## Why No Retrieval Targets Are Needed\n\nThe first two Introduction paragraphs (`paper.tex:17`) and the protection rationale in Method (`paper.tex:64`) lack local literature citations, but their substantive background is already covered by the cited selection-and-assessment literature in Related Work. Reusing those existing citations could improve placement; it does not require retrieving additional references.\n\nThe Wilson construction in Method (`paper.tex:71`) and Supplementary Information (`paper.tex:292`) is conventional and has relevant existing coverage in Brown. The recorded bootstrap implementation is described as descriptive and unvalidated, not positioned as a new or guaranteed procedure. Neither warrants an additional literature pass on the current wording.\n\nQuantitative findings, comparator definitions, model configuration, and implementation details have supplied result or source grounding. They are not missing-literature targets. The finite-audit caveats and limitations restrict the claims rather than asserting external benchmark rankings or population guarantees. Expanding into adaptive prompt generation, new allocation policies, or unmeasured systems would reshape the study instead of repairing a paragraph-specific citation gap.\n\n## Decision\n\n- Missing literatures: none.\n- Rewrite targets: none.\n- Recommended post-draft retrieval: skip.\n- Failure reason: none.\n\nThis decision concerns citation-gap triage, not a full bibliographic metadata audit or independent validation of every cited result. The manuscript and existing reference files remain unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
